a52sxq audio: fixes from the 2026-11-18 audit (logs/audit-2026-11-18.json)

Apply inside audio-kernel/ with patch -p1 (after the other a52-*.patch files).

- asoc/msm-pcm-afe-v2.c: AFE proxy copy() did memcpy on the struct iov_iter
  itself; use copy_{from,to}_iter and check the byte count.
- asoc/msm-pcm-q6-noirq.c: MMAP_DATA_FD leaked a file reference (fget never
  put) and set FMODE_WRITE after the fd was published.
- asoc/lahaina.c: FE QoS vote counted once per FE stream instead of once per
  prepare; /proc/asound/cardN/state (5.4 QGKI entry the HAL's sndmonitor
  polls) recreated in the machine driver and driven from the SSR callbacks.
- asoc/codecs/wcd938x/wcd938x.c: probe error paths and remove hold reset low
  and disable the static supplies (regulator_put WARN per probe deferral).
- asoc/codecs/tas256x: irq_work no longer leaves codec_lock held when it runs
  while suspended; suspend cancels the work outside the lock; the skipped
  work is re-run at resume.
- asoc/codecs/bolero/{rx,tx,wsa}-macro.c: defer until bolero-clk-rsc-mngr
  has registered (6.12 board DT lists it last).
- dsp/q6voice.c: voice_map_cal_memory() uses its own cal_map_lock instead of
  common_lock (self-deadlock from voc_register_vocproc_vol_table);
  voc_disable_device() tests the real result of the CMA cal reclaim.
- dsp/msm_audio_ion.c: no list_mutex self-deadlock when the kernel mapping
  fails; balance begin_cpu_access when vmap fails.
- soc/swr-mstr-ctrl.c: runtime resume returns 0 on a failed core vote, as on
  5.4 (a non-zero return latches runtime_error for good).
- ipc/apr.c: all local setup (apr_cb_work, TAL, snd_event client) before
  joining the ADSP notifier chain; apr_debug_init no longer __init.
- dsp/adsp-loader.c: restart requests use rproc_report_crash() (real SSR as
  5.4 subsystem_restart_dev) instead of dropping one rproc power reference.
- asoc/codecs/wcd938x/wcd938x-mbhc.c: surge protection re-enabled on every
  Z-det exit.
- asoc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c: Samsung's MAX_IMPED guard restored (a floating
  Z-det reading is not a line-out).

